    10	- `hosts/shared/layout-btrfs.env` or `hosts/shared/layout-f2fs.env`
    11	- `hosts/shared/boot.env`
    12	- optional profile override envs under `hosts/profiles/override/<name>.env`
    13	
    14	The loader assembles the concrete host policy env in this order:
    15	
    16	1. `hosts/profiles/<family>/<role>.env` or `hosts/profiles/override/<name>.env`
    17	2. `hosts/shared/identity.env`
    18	3. `hosts/shared/runtime.env`
    19	4. `hosts/shared/server.env` for server profiles only
    20	5. `hosts/shared/layout.env`
    21	6. `hosts/shared/layout-<storage-family>.env`
    22	7. `hosts/shared/boot.env`
    23	
    24	Account policy is loaded separately from `hosts/shared/account.env`.
    25	Desktop profiles own their complete Labwc and desktop-addon policy directly;
    26	there is no shared desktop env layer.
    27	
    28	When the optional `profile` class group is selected, the matching
    29	`hosts/profiles/override/<name>.env` replaces the normal
    30	`hosts/profiles/<family>/<role>.env` source while the remaining shared
    31	cross-role and layout layers continue to load in the same order.
    32	
    33	The concrete profile loads first because shared env files derive tmpfs, zram,
    34	device, GRUB, server addon policy, sysctl, and installed static
    35	networking policy from the role-specific `SIZE_*`, `BOOTPROFILE_*`, `GRUB_*`,
    36	`WIFI_*`, `TAILSCALE_*`, `SYNCTHING_*`, and slot values owned by the selected
    37	profile. Installed-system log levels are shared policy in `shared/runtime.env`.
    38	For the `tailscale` addon, the concrete profile owns the node-side Tailscale
    39	policy defaults such as tag advertisement, route advertisement, operator user,
    40	approval-sensitive auth-key requirements, daemon retry behavior, and the
    41	managed bootstrap timeout. Shipped profiles require an injected auth key so
    42	unattended installs cannot silently leave Tailscale stopped.
    43	`hosts/shared/layout.env` carries only cross-family mount primitives and
    44	tmpfs/dm-crypt backing policy; `layout-btrfs.env` and `layout-f2fs.env` own
    45	their layout labels, mount, mkfs, formatter sizing, and GRUB root policy.
    46	In the F2FS family, `/pool` remains ext4 and therefore uses `MNT_EXT4_POOL_OPTS`.
    47	Static target IPv4/IPv6 addresses are no longer stored in host profiles. The
    48	installed static network handoff now derives its concrete address, netmask,
    49	gateway, and nameserver values directly from installer kernel cmdline answers
    50	(`netcfg/get_*` plus optional `ipv6_*`).
    51	Installed-system log defaults in `shared/runtime.env` are intentionally sparse:
    52	nftables defaults to `none`, while zram and systemd/network helpers default to
    53	`error`.
    54	`NFTABLES_LOG_LEVEL` controls generator diagnostic output only; packet logging
    55	is controlled by nftables profile or service overlay `logging.*.enabled`
    56	fields, not by log level.
    57	`NFTABLES_LOG_LEVEL`, `ZRAM_LOG_LEVEL`, and `SYSTEMD_LOG_LEVEL` accept
